    "result_text": "All 267 tests pass, including the new `Cp06Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that an owner's response include a `displayName` field formatted as `\"LastName, FirstName\"`. Since the acceptance test creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` and reads the field back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, I computed it as a derived (read-only) field on the DTO so both paths return it consistently.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (regenerating `OwnerDto` with the new field at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field from the entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nDeriving it in the mapper (rather than storing it on the entity) means it's always current and requires no new function step in the OfficeFloor POST pipeline \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated` and `RespondWithOwner` responders both go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`.",
